    "text": "A fluid is flowing through a horizontal pipe of varying cross-section, with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;at a point where the pressure is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;Pascal. At another point where pressure&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;Pascal its speed is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the density of the fluid is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and the flow is streamline, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to&nbsp;"
  },
